{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794304667,"nonce":"c1vU1JD0044KoL/THdqoWOzKP2Q=","title":"No p-adaptivity for Nedelec (H(curl)) fields","message":"jno.solve.enrich adapts a space='cover' field: a first-order physical cover per node on a simplex mesh, which spans P2 locally and blends through the partition of unity. That is an H1 (nodal) construction. A Nedelec field has one degree for the whole field (order= on fem_symbols), so a time-harmonic Maxwell cell cannot raise the order only where the field is rough (in a metal skin, at a hole edge). Needed: variable degree per cell for N1E (hierarchical edge/face/interior modes with the minimum rule on shared edges and faces), or an H(curl)-conforming cover enrichment, plus an estimator for H(curl) fields (see the adaptive-loop estimator issue).","files":null}]}